  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communications plan on UNESCO / RCU partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AlUla, located in north-west Saudi Arabia, is rich in its cultural and natural heritage, with ancient sites dating back thousands of years. Today, it stands witness to the influence of various civilizations, showcasing the legacy of important cultural exchanges, demonstrating the rich history of the region. Yet it remains largely unknown worldwide. This Partnership is an opportunity to strenghten UNESCO&apos;s visibility for the protection of a major World Heritage Site, enhance trans sectoral activity and boost digital content, notably in Arabic and for the middle east region.</narrative>
  </description>
